From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:37:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wifi: mt76: reset operating channel survey on software
 scan

__mt76_set_channel() clears chan_state only when tuning to a channel
other than main_chandef.chan. As a result, a software scan (including
ACS when a radio is restarted) finds the operating channel with hours
of accumulated active, busy, TX, and BSS-RX history, while every other
channel covers only the scan dwell. Traffic from the AP's own clients
then makes the current channel look busy compared to idle channels.

In mt76_sw_scan(), take dev->mutex, fold any pending hardware counters
and elapsed time into the current state via mt76_update_survey(), and
then zero the main channel's chan_state under dev->cc_lock (matching
mt7603_mac_tx_stats and mt76x02_update_channel() which update cc_tx
under cc_lock). Reading MT_MIB_STAT_CCA (mt7603, clear-on-read) and
MT_CH_BUSY (mt76x2, read-and-clear) inside mt76_update_survey() before
zeroing chan_state ensures no counts are lost or double-counted across
the scan boundary.

Side effects checked across image consumers:
- Only `iw ... survey dump` shows the operating channel's counters
  since the last scan (ACS, LuCI scan button, or travelmate WISP scan)
  rather than since boot; /usr/bin/iwinfo (a ucode script) has no
  survey command, and libiwinfo (libiwinfo.so.20230701) and iwinfo.uc
  (rpcd-mod-iwinfo) read only the noise.
- LuCI wireless.js reads only noise from GET_SURVEY; LuCI scan and
  travelmate/wpa_supplicant read scan results, not survey busy time.
- hostapd BSS Load (when bss_load_update_period is enabled) computes
  deltas only when channel_time increases, so a reset skips one interval
  and resyncs cleanly.
---
 mac80211.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
index 7d27f952..7755e71b 100644
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1968,6 +1968,19 @@ void mt76_sw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 		  const u8 *mac)
 {
 	struct mt76_phy *phy = hw->priv;
+	struct mt76_dev *dev = phy->dev;
+
+	mutex_lock(&dev->mutex);
+	mt76_update_survey(phy);
+	if (phy->main_chandef.chan) {
+		struct mt76_channel_state *state;
+
+		state = mt76_channel_state(phy, phy->main_chandef.chan);
+		spin_lock_bh(&dev->cc_lock);
+		memset(state, 0, sizeof(*state));
+		spin_unlock_bh(&dev->cc_lock);
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&dev->mutex);
 
 	set_bit(MT76_SCANNING, &phy->state);
 }
